the knowledge base facility_agreement includes:

% 1.1 Definition (form definition)
“Borrower” means the company named as borrower in the schedule.

% 1.2 Definition (form definition)
“Lender” means each bank listed in Part 1 of the schedule.

% 1.3 Definition (form definition)
“Loan” means a loan made or to be made under the Facility.

% 1.4 Definition (form definition)
“Facility” means the term loan facility made available under this Agreement.

% 1.5 Definition (form definition)
“Repayment Date” means the date falling five years after the date of this Agreement.

% 2.1 Obligation (form obligation)
Lender shall make available to Borrower a term loan facility in an aggregate amount equal to GBP 10,000,000.

% 2.2 Permission (form permission)
Borrower may cancel the whole or any part of the Facility on not less than five Business Days' prior notice.

% 3.1 Obligation (form pay-interest-at-rate)
Borrower shall pay interest on each Loan at 2.5 per cent per annum.

% 3.2 Obligation (keyword)
Interest shall be calculated on the basis of a 365 day year.

% 4.1 Obligation (form obligation)
Borrower shall repay each Loan in full on the Repayment Date.

% 4.2 Obligation (form obligation)
Borrower shall pay a prepayment fee of GBP 250 for each prepayment.

% 5.1 Prohibition (form prohibition)
Borrower shall not create any security over its assets.

% 5.2 Obligation (form obligation)
Borrower shall supply its annual financial statements to the [Agent] within 120 days of each financial year end.

% 6.1 Power (form power-on-condition)
If Borrower does not pay any sum due under this Agreement, Lender may declare all Loans immediately due.

% 6.2 Deeming (form deemed-shall)
A Loan shall be deemed due on the date a demand is made.
